  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company returned to top‑line growth, supported by accelerating billings and larger deal sizes. Demand for Rimini Support and the Smart Path offering remains solid, while early uptake of new agentic AI solutions is adding momentum. The drag from the legacy PeopleSoft runoff continues, but underlying ex‑PeopleSoft momentum is healthier. However, growth investments are pressuring margins, creating a mixed picture of improving demand overshadowed by near‑term profitability compression.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is leaning heavily into front‑loaded investments around Rimini Agentic AI ERP, targeting larger clients without requiring migrations. The EPS miss signals tight execution scrutiny, even as the team highlights accelerating pipeline and a strong bookings trend. Credibility hinges on converting early AI momentum into sustained top‑line acceleration while eventually restoring margin leverage. The trimmed fair‑value estimate reflects cautious optimism about execution rather than a change in the long‑term story.",
